hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5446","Muhammad bin Adam told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “There were three cases in Barira. Its people wanted to sell it and required loyalty. I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her. She said: And she was freed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her the choice. So she chose herself, and he used to give her in charity and she would give us some of it as a gift. I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Eat it, for it is... It is due as charity, and it is a gift to us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5447","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I bought Barira, and its people stipulated that she be loyal, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Free her, for loyalty is to the one who gives The paper. She said: So I freed her. She said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, summoned her and gave her a choice over her husband. She said: If he gave me such and such. Likewise, when I stayed with him, she chose herself, and her husband was free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5448","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, he is the son of the Mahdi. He said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “She wanted to buy Bareerah, so they stipulated her loyalty. I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her and brings the meat. It was said that this is among what is given in charity to Barira, so he said: It is “She gets charity and we get a gift. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her the choice, and her husband was free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5449","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said “I charged Barirah for nine uqiyahs each year for an uqiyah, so she came to Aisha asking for her help, and she said: Unless they want to.” I will prepare it for them all at once, and the loyalty will be mine. So Bareerah went and spoke about that to her family, but they refused to do so unless it was... Loyalty to them, so she came to Aisha, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came at that time, and she said to her: What, her family said, She said: No, by God, then, unless the loyalty is to me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is this? She said: O Messenger of God, indeed Bareerah came to me asking me for her help to write it down, so I said: No, unless they want me to prepare it for them all at once and the loyalty is to me, so she mentioned. That was for its owners, but they refused to give it anything except that the allegiance be to them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Buy it and make a stipulation for them. Loyalty, for loyalty belongs to the one who is freed, then he gets up and addresses the people, praising God and praising Him, then he says: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions? It is not in the Book of God Almighty. They say, “I free so-and-so and allegiance is to me.” The Book of God Almighty is more worthy, and the condition of God is more reliable, and every condition is not in the Book of God Almighty. The Book of God is invalid, and if there were a hundred conditions, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a choice over her husband, and he was a slave, so she chose herself.” Urwah said: If he had been free, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not have given her a choice."
"5450","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Salamah told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, On the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “Barira’s husband was a slave.”"
"5451","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “She bought Bureerah from some of the Ansar, and they stipulated loyalty, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Loyalty is to the one who is bestowed with blessings, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her the choice, and her husband was a slave, and she gave Aisha meat, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If you give us some of this meat, Aisha said: Give it in charity to Barira, and he said: It is her responsibility. charity, and it is a gift to us.”"
"5452","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Ulayya informed us, saying: Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, he said: He was his father’s executor. He said: I would rather say: I heard it from your father. Aisha said, “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Barira, and I wanted to buy it and stipulate loyalty to its people. He said: Buy her, for loyalty belongs to the one who emancipates. He said: She was given the choice, and her husband was a slave. Then he said after that: I do not know. I do not know. And he will come. Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with meat. They said: This is what she gave in charity to Bareerah. He said: It is charity for her, and for us it is a gift. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5453","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam Al-Basri told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, he said: Abu Yafour told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Duhaa, he said: We discussed the month with him, and some of us said: thirty, and some of us said: twenty-nine, so Abu Al-Duhaa said: Ibn Abbas narrated to us, He said: “One morning, the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were crying, and each woman had her own family with them. So I entered the mosque, and behold... It was full of people. He said: Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, came and went up to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in his upper room, and he greeted him. No one answered him. Then he greeted him and no one answered him. He returned and called Bilal. He went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Have you divorced your wives? He said: No, but I was with them for a month, so he stayed for twenty-nine days, then he came down and entered upon Aisha.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5454","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had some of his wives.” He stayed for twenty-nine nights, then came down, and it was said: O Messenger of God, didn’t you intend to spend a month? He said: The month \twenty-nine\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5455","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had intercourse with his wife and he had intercourse with her. He said: O Messenger of God, “I I had intercourse with my wife, and I fell upon her before I made amends. He said: What made you do that, may God have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklets in the light? The moon, and he said: Do not approach it until you have done what God Almighty has commanded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5456","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, He said: “A man pretended to be with his wife and had intercourse with her before he made amends. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him, May God bless him and grant him peace: What made you do that? He said: May God have mercy on you, O Messenger of God. I saw her anklets or her legs in the moonlight. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: So stay away from her until you do what God Almighty has commanded you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5457","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh informed us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir informed us, and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala Al-San’ani informed us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Al-Hakam, saying: I heard Ikrimah, “that a man said: O Messenger of God, he has had intercourse with his wife. Then he cheated on her before he did what he had to do. He said: What made you do that? He said: I saw the whites of her legs in the moon. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Then stay away from her until she has fulfilled what is due to you.” The word is for Muhammad. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The mursal is more correct than the musnad, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5458","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “Praise be to God, whose hearing encompasses voices. Khawla came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining Her husband, and her words were hidden from me, so God Almighty revealed, “God has heard the words of the woman who disputes with you about her husband and complains to God.” And God hears your conversation.”"
"5459","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Al-Makhzoumi, who is Al-Mughirah bin Salamah, told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “The women who are extracted and the women who are divorced are the hypocritical women.” Al-Hasan said: I did not hear it from anyone except Abu Hurairah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan did not hear anything from Abu Hurairah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5460","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Masry informed us, saying: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Amra bint Abd Al-Rahman said that she told him, on the authority of Habiba bint Sahl, “that she was under the rule of Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, went out in the morning and found Habiba bint Sahl at his door in the morning. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who This one? She said: I am Habiba bint Sahl, O Messenger of God. He said: What is the matter with you? She said: Neither I nor Thabit bin Qays for her husband. When Thabit bin Qais came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: This is Habiba bint Sahl, who has mentioned what God willed that she should mention. Then Habiba said: O Messenger of God, I have everything he gave me. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Thabit: Take from her, so he took from it and sat among its people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5461","5506 Azhar bin Jamil Al-Basri told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he is Al-Thaqafi bin Abdul Majeed, he said: Khaled told us, he is Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the wife of Thabit ibn Qais came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God Thabit bin Qais said, “As for me, I do not blame him for his character or religion, but I hate disbelief in Islam.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you want to give him back his garden? She said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Accept the garden, and divorce her once. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5462","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My wife does not withhold the hand of someone who touches her. He said: Leave it alone. He said: I fear that my soul will follow it. He said: Enjoy it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5463","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Harun bin Riyab informed us. On the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of God, “Below me is a beautiful woman who does not withhold a hand.” He touched her. He said: Divorce her. He said: I cannot be patient with her. He said: Then he kept her. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: An-Nadr ibn Shumayl differed concerning him. It was narrated by others, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Harun bin Riab, and Abdul Karim Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Umair, Abdul Karim said, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. Abdul Karim is not that strong, and Harun bin Ri’ab is trustworthy, and Harun’s hadith is more authentic, and Harun sent him."
"5464","On the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of his uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: “I was having a wife whom Omar hated, so he said: Divorce her, but I refused: so Omar came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Obey your father.”"
"5465","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi, whose name is Suleiman bin Dawud, told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us Ibn Abi Salamah, and Ibrahim Ibn Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Saad, on the authority of Asim Ibn Adi, who said: “Uwaimir, a man from Bani Al-Ajlan, and he said: O Asim, have you seen a man who saw a man with his wife and killed him? You kill him, or how does he do it, O Asim? This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he asked Asim about this Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he criticized the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He disliked the issues and he hated them. Then Uwaimir came to him and said: What did you do, Asim? He said: What did you do? You did not bring me anything good. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked about the issues and criticized them. Uwaymer said: By God, I will ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. So he went to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He asked him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: God Almighty has revealed this about you and your companion, so bring it. Sahl said: I was with the people with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he brought it, and we talked and said: O Messenger of God, by God, if I caught her, I lied to her, so he left her before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to separate from her, so it became the custom of the cursed. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5466","Ahmad bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, he said: Omar bin Ali told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed between Al-Ajlani and his wife, and she was Pregnant (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5467","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Abd al-A’la, he is the sublime son of Abd al-A’la, told us: Hisham was asked about A man slanders his wife. Hisham, meaning Ibn Hassan, told us on the authority of Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Anas Ibn Malik about that. And I see that he has knowledge of that, so he said: “Hilal bin Umayyah slandered his wife with Sharik bin Al-Sahma’, and he was the brother of Al-Baraa bin Malik to his mother, and he was the first to curse, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed between them, then said: Look at him, and if she brought him white A sheep with brown eyes, then it belongs to Hilal ibn Umayyah, and if she brings it with kohl-colored, curly, red-legged hair, then it belongs to Sharik ibn al-Sahma’,” he said. So I was informed that she brought him with kohl-coloured hair and blackened legs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5468","Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Husayn al-Azdi told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: “The first li’an in Islam was that Hilal ibn Umayyah slandered Sharik ibn al-Sahma’ with his wife, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace. So he informed him of that, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Four martyrs, otherwise there will be someone at your back repeating: This happened to him repeatedly, and Hilal said to him: By God, O Messenger of God, God Almighty knows that I am telling the truth, and may God Almighty know that I am telling the truth. You have to do what will free my back from the punishment. While they were like that, the verse of cursing was revealed to him. And those who accuse their wives, to the last of the verses. So he called Hilal, and he bore four testimonies by God that he is of the truthful, and the fifth is that the curse of God is upon him if he is of the liars, then The woman was called and she testified four times that God is one of the liars. When he was four or five years old, the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Stop her, for it is obligatory. She delayed until we doubted that she would confess, then she said: I will not expose my people. The rest of the day, then she went on the right, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Look for her, and if she brings him a white, young man. The eyes, then it belongs to Hilal ibn Umayyah, and if she brings it to Adam with a quarter of a wrinkled head, then it belongs to Sharik ibn al-Sahma’, so she brought it Adam curled up a quarter of his legs, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Were it not for what had preceded in it from the Book of God, I and her would have had an affair. And the one with short eyes: long on the eyelids, neither wide-eyed nor protruding. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5469","Issa bin Hammad told us, Zaghba, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Qasim Bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: Cursing was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Asim bin Adi said something about that. Then he left, and a man from his people came to him, complaining to him that he had found a man with his wife. Asim said: I was not afflicted with this except by saying: So he took it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told him what he found his wife doing, and that man was yellowish, slightly Meat, full of hair, and the one who claimed that he found it with his family was a lean man with a lot of meat. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Oh God, make it clear. So she gave birth to someone resembling the man whom her husband mentioned that he found with her, so he cursed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Between them, a man said to Ibn Abbas in the assembly: Is it the one that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I stoned anyone without proof, I would be stoned. This? Ibn Abbas said: No, that is a woman who used to show bad behavior in Islam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5470","Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ja’far, on the authority of Yahya, he said: I heard Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim narrates, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that he said: “Cursing was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace be upon him, and Asim bin Adi said something about that, then he left, and a man from his people met him, and he mentioned that he was found with his wife. A man, so he took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told him what he found his wife doing, and that man was turning yellow. He was of little meat and had unruly hair, and the one against whom it was claimed was that he found among his family a destitute human being, a lot of flesh, and frizzy, so the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Oh God, explain. So she gave birth similar to the one her husband mentioned that he found with her, so curse the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. peace be upon him, and a man said to Ibn Abbas in the assembly: Is it the one that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I stoned anyone without Is this woman stoned? Ibn Abbas said: No, that is a woman who showed evil in Islam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5471","Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He commanded a man, when he commanded those who are being cursed to curse us, to place his hand on his throat at the fifth hour, and he said: It is obligatory.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5472","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: I was asked about the two cursers, in the emirate of Ibn al-Zubayr. Is there a difference between them? I did not know what to say, so I got up from my place to Ibn Omar's house, and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, the two cursed people, can there be a difference between them? He said: Yes, Glory be to God. The first person to be asked about that was so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, and he said: O Messenger of God, have you seen? Amr did not say: Have you seen? The man among us finds his wife obscene. If he speaks, it will be a great matter. And Amr said: He has committed a great matter, but if he remains silent, he will remain silent about a proverb. He did not answer him, but after that he came to him and said: I have been tested with the matter with which I asked you, so God Almighty revealed these verses. In Surah An-Nur: And those who accuse their wives, until he reached the fifth time that God’s wrath be upon her if he were of the truthful ones, so he began with the man. So he advised him, reminded him, and told him that the torment of this world is lesser than the torment of the hereafter, so he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not lie, then He praised the woman, and he advised her and reminded her, and she said: By the one who sent you with the truth, he is indeed a liar. So he started with the man, so he bore witness four times. Testimonies of God that he is one of the truthful, and the fifth is that the curse of God is upon him if he is one of the liars, then he mentions the woman and bears witness. “Four testimonies of God that he is one of the liars, and the fifth is that God was angry with her if he were truthful, so He separated between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5473","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, and the pronunciation is his, they said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Al-Mu’sab did not differentiate between the two who curse each other. Sa’id said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Umar, and he said: “The Messenger of God made a distinction.” May God bless him and grant him peace between the two brothers of Banu Al-Ajlan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5474","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: “He slandered A man and his wife, and he said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, separated between the two brothers of Banu Al-Ajlan, and said: God knows that one of you is a liar. “Amr ibn Dinar said to me: There is something in this hadith that I do not see you narrating. He said: The man said: My money. He said: You have no money. If you are truthful, then you have access to it, and if you are lying, then it is further away from you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5475","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: I asked Ibn Umar about Those who are cursed, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those who are cursed: “Your reckoning is with God. One of you is a liar, and you have no way over her. He said: O Messenger of God, what is wrong with me? He said: You have no money. If you told the truth about her, then it is because of what you made of her private parts permissible, but if you lied to her, that is farther for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5476","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed among A man and his wife, and separated them, and joined the child to the mother.”"
"5477","5521 Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from Banu Fazara came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My wife gave birth to a black boy.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do you have any camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colours? He said: Are there any that are pink? He said: Yes There was a leaf in it. He said: How do you see that? He said: Perhaps it was removed by sweat. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This may be the case. It will be removed by sweat.”"
"5478","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: A man from Bani Fazara came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My wife has given birth to a boy Black, and he wanted to get rid of it. He said: Do you have any camels? He said: Yes. He said: What color are they? He said: Red. He said: Are there any in them? He said: It has a leafy mane. He said: What is that? He said: Perhaps it was removed by a vein. He said: Perhaps this is what it removed. race, and he was not permitted to be free from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5479","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah informed us, he said: Abu Haywa al-Humsi, whose name is Shurayh ibn Yazid, informed us, he said: Shuaib ibn Abi informed us. Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he rose A man. He said: O Messenger of God, a black boy was born to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How did that happen? He said: I do not know. He said: Do you have any camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colours? He said: Are there camels that are green? He said: How did that happen? He said: I do not know, O Messenger of God, unless it was removed by sweat. He said: This is perhaps caused by sweat, so that is why. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled this: “It is not permissible for a man to deny birth to a child born in his bed, unless he claims that he saw \obscene\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5480","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yunus. On the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying, “When a verse was revealed The cursed woman: Any woman who introduces a man to a people who is not from them, she is not of God in anything, and He will not admit her to His Paradise, and any man who denies His son, and as he looked at him, God Almighty hid himself from him, and exposed him to the heads of the first and the last.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5481","5525 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “The child is for the bed, and the stone is for the prostitute.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5482","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The child is for the bed, and the stone is for the prostitute.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5483","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Saad bin disputed Abi Waqqas and Abd bin Zamaa with a boy. Saad said: This, O Messenger of God, is the son of my brother Utbah bin Abi Waqqas. He entrusted me that he His son, look at his likeness, and Abd bin Zam’a said: My brother was born on my father’s bed by his daughter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at To his resemblance, and he saw a clear resemblance to a threshold, so he said: He is yours, O slave. The child is for the bed, and the whore is for the stone, and hide from him, O slave. Sawda bint Zamaa, he had never seen Sawda.”"
"5484","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh informed us, saying: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yusuf bin al-Zubayr, a servant To them, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: “Zam’ah had a slave girl whom he had intercourse with, and he was thinking about another that he was intercourse with her, so she came.” With a son similar to the one she had thought of, and Zam’ah died while she was pregnant, so Sawda mentioned this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The child is for the bed, so hide from him, woman, for you have no brother.”"
"5485","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The child is for the bed, and the stone is for the prostitute.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not think this is on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Masoud, and God Almighty knows best"
"5486","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Saad bin Abi disputed Waqqas, and Abd bin Zam’a, regarding Ibn Zam’a, and Saad said: “My brother Utbah advised me: If you come to Mecca, see Ibn Zam’a’s servant. He is my son, and Abd bin Zam’a said: He is the son of my father’s maidservant. He was born on my father’s bed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw something similar to it. We showed Utbah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The child is for the bed, and cover yourself from him, O Sawda.”"
"5487","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram informed us, he said: Abdul Razzaq informed us, he said: Al-Thawri informed us, on the authority of Saleh Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, said: “Three things were brought to Ali, may God be pleased with him, while he was in Yemen. They fell upon a woman in One man became pure, so he asked two: Will you marry this child? They said: No. Then he asked two: Will you marry this child? They said: No, so he cast lots He assigned the child to the one for whom the lot had been drawn, and imposed two-thirds of the blood money on him. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He laughed until his molars became visible.” Ali bin Hajar al-Marwazi told us, saying: Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of al-Ajlah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, He said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Khalil Al-Hadrami informed me, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam. He said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, A man came from Yemen and started telling him and Ali about it, so he said: O Messenger of God, three people came to Ali and were disputing about a son. “They had sexual intercourse with a woman while she was in purity,” and the hadith stems from (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5488","Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs told us, he said: Yahya told us, he is Al-Qattan, he said: Al-Ajlah told us, and his name is Yahya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, on that day. In Yemen, a man came to him and said: “I witnessed Ali being brought in three people who claimed to have given birth to a woman. Ali said to one of them: Are you leaving him for this? He refused.” He said to this man: Will you leave him for this, but he refused? He said to this man: Will you leave him for this, but he refused. Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Are you partners? They are quarreling, and I will cast lots among you. Whichever of you gets the lot is his, and he must pay two-thirds of the blood money. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. And he bowed until his molars became visible.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: These hadiths are all with mixed chains of narration. Ishaq ibn Shaheen told us. He is Al-Wasiti. He said: Khaled told us: He is Ibn Abdullah Al-Wasiti Al-Tahan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of a man from Hadramaut. On the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Ali to Yemen, and a boy was brought over whom three quarreled with. The hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Salama bin Kuhayl disagreed with them. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning a gendarme. Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, he said: I heard Shu’bi speaking, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, or Ibn Abi al-Khalil, “that three people “Participate in purification.” He mentioned something similar, but did not mention Zayd bin Arqam and did not narrate it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Salamah bin Kuhayl I confirm them, and his hadith is more correct than that, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5489","5534 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He came to me happily, the secrets of his face shining, and he said: Did you not see that Mujazzi looked at Zayd ibn Harithah and Usama?” Ibn Zaid, and he said: Some of these feet belong to others."
"5490","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me one day happily, and said: O Aisha, did you not see that Mujazz al-Mudaliji entered? Ali and I were with Usama bin Zaid, and he saw Usama bin Zaid and Zaid, wearing velvet, and they had covered their heads, and their feet were exposed. He said: These are feet one from another."
"5491","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Sufyan is Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Othman Al-Batti, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Salamah al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “He converted to Islam, and his wife refused to convert to Islam, so their son came A child who had not yet reached puberty, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the father sit here and the mother here, then he gave him a choice and said: O God, guide him, so he went. \to his father\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5492","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ziyad told me He is Ibn Saad, on the authority of Hilal ibn Usama, on the authority of Abu Maimuna, and his name. They said: Sulaym. He said: While I was with Abu Hurairah, he said: “Indeed A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. My husband wants to go with my son, and he has helped me. He gave me a drink from the well of Abu Anabah, and her husband came and said: Who will dispute with me regarding my son? He said: O boy, this is your father, and this is your mother. So take by the hand whichever one you wish.” So he took his mother’s hand and she took him off. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5493","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Shazan bin Othman, brother of Abdan, told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman informed me that Al-Rabi’ bint Mu’awiz bin Afraa told him that Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas “hit his wife and broke her hand, and she was Jamila bint Abdullah bin Ubayy, so he came Her brother complained about him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for Thabit, and said to him: Take the You have the right to her, and let her go. He said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to wait for one menstrual period and join her. \With its people\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5494","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: my uncle told us, he said: my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: he told me Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh, who said: I said to her: Tell me your hadith. She said: “I broke away from My husband, then I went to Uthman and asked him what I must do regarding the waiting period. He said: You do not have to wait until you are recently married to him, so you should stay until that time. She menstruates. She said: “Indeed, the decree of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was followed in that regard regarding Maryam Al-Mughaliya. She was married to Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, so it was taken away from him.”"
"5495","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Humayd bin Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Habibah: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn a dead person over Three days, except for four months and ten days.”"
"5496","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani informed us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Humaid ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab, I said: On the authority of her mother, he said: Yes, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about a woman whose husband died, and they feared for her eyes. Should she apply kohl? He said: One of you was staying in her house in her bad mood for a year, so when he passed by, she threw a dung, then left, but there were no four. \months and tens\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5497","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed bin Qais bin Qahd Al-Ansari, and he found that he had realized The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Humayd ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah, who said: She came A woman went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “My daughter’s husband has died, and I fear for her eyes. Should I apply kohl to her?” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of you has been sitting for a year, but it has only been four months and ten days, so if One year old, she went out and left behind her a dumping ground. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5498","Muhammad Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: I heard Yahya, he is the son of Saeed Al-Ansari, he said: I heard Nafi’, on the authority of Safiya bint Abi Ubaid, that she heard Hafsa bint Omar, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No.” It is permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband, in which case she mourns him for four months. \And ten\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5499","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah Al-Attar Al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sawa told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day, and believes in God and His Messenger, to mourn more than three dead people.” days, except for a pair, for it is a period of four months and ten days for him.” Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim told me, he said: Tell us Al-Sahmi, whose name is Abdullah bin Bakr bin Habib, said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she is Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5500","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us, reading it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is by Muhammad, saying: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Subayah Al-Aslamiyah “fell asleep a few nights after her husband’s death, so she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she asked him for permission to get married, so he gave her permission, so she got married.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5501","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dawud, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar, and he Ibn Makhramah said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “commanded Subay’ah to get married if she became ill from postpartum.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5502","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi informed me, he said: Jarir informed me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu al-Sanabel, he said : Subayah gave birth twenty-three or twenty-five nights after her husband’s death, and when she became pregnant, she longed for husbands, so it is shameful. That is for her, so it was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Whatever prevents her, her time has passed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5503","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abu Dawud, who is Al-Tayalisi, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abd told me Rabbuh bin Saeed said: I heard Abu Salamah saying: Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas differed regarding the woman whose husband died if she gave birth. He carried her. Abu Hurairah said: He got married. Ibn Abbas said: After the two terms, so they sent to Umm Salamah, and she said: Subay’a’s husband has died. She gave birth fifteen and a half months after the death of her husband. She said: Two men proposed to her, so she bound herself to one of them. When They feared that she might break away by herself. They said: You are not permissible. She said: So she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You are permissible. So marry whomever you want.”"
"5504","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us, reading it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is by Muhammad, he said: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of the servant of his Lord. Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Abdullah Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah were asked about the woman whose husband died while she was pregnant. Ibn Saeed said Abbas: The last of the two terms, and Abu Hurairah said: If she gives birth, then she is permissible. So Abu Salamah went to Umm Salamah and asked her about that, and she said: Subayah al-Aslamiya was born half a month after her husband’s death, and two men proposed to her, one of them a young man and the other an old man. She was proposed to The young man, and the old man said: She is not permissible and her family was absent, so he hoped that when her family came they would give him preference over her, so she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “You are permissible, so marry whomever you want.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5505","Zakaria ibn Yahya al-Sijistani informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, he is the son of Rahawayh, informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn informed us. Ibn Waqid, he said: My father told me, he said: Yazid the grammarian informed us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “What We abrogate from a verse or cause it to be forgotten, and We bring something better than it or something similar to it. And God Almighty says: And when We change a verse in place of another verse, and God knows best what He descends, and the Almighty said: God erases what He wills and establishes it, and with Him is the Mother of the Book, so the first thing that was abrogated from the Qur’an was the qiblah, and the Almighty said: Divorced women should wait for three menstrual periods, and God Almighty said: And those of your women who have given up on menstruation, if you are in doubt, then you should complete their waiting period. Three months, then it was abrogated from that. The Almighty said: If you marry believing women and then divorce them before you have touched them, then what is yours? “on them from a number of times that you transgress.”"
"5506","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told me, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Hajjaj, who is the Sufi, told us, he said: told us Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: It was said to Ibn Abbas about a woman who gave birth after the death of her husband. In twenty nights: Is it appropriate for her to get married? He said: No, except the last of the two terms. I said: God, Blessed and Most High, said: And those who are pregnant are their time to give birth, so He said: Only that. Concerning divorce, Abu Hurairah said, “I am with my nephew,” meaning: Abu Salamah. So he sent his servant Kurayb, and he said: Go to Umm Salamah, and ask her: Was it Is this a Sunnah from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he came to him and said: She said: Yes, Subay’ah al-Aslamiyah. She gave birth twenty nights after her husband’s death, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her to give birth. “May God’s peace and blessings be upon him,” he said, “and Abu al-Sanabel was among those who proposed to her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5507","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that Abu Hurairah, Ibn Abbas and Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman remembered the waiting period for a woman who died. A pregnant woman gives birth when her husband dies. Ibn Abbas said: Abbas: She must wait for the last of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: Rather, she is permissible when she gives birth. Abu Hurairah said, “I am with my brother’s son.” So they sent for Umm Salamah. The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Subayah al-Aslamiya gave birth shortly after the death of her husband. So she consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so he commanded her to get married.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5508","Abd al-A'la bin Wasil bin Abd al-A'la informed us, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Umm Salamah, and Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said “Subay’ah gave birth a few days after her husband’s death, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to get married.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5509","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that Abdullah bin Abbas and Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman disagreed about whether a woman should breathe several nights after the death of her husband. Abdullah bin Abbas said: The last of the two deadlines, and Abu Salamah said: If it is finished, then it is permissible. Then Abu Hurairah came and said, “I am with my nephew,” meaning: Abu Salamah. So they sent Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, went to Umm Salamah to ask her about that. He came to them and told them that she said: “Subay’ah gave birth to A few nights after the death of her husband, she mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5510","Hussein bin Mansour bin Ja’far al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Yahya bin Sa’id told us, he said: Suleiman bin Yassar told me, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: It was me, Ibn Abbas, and Abu Hurairah, so Ibn Abbas: If a woman gives birth after the death of her husband, then her waiting period is the last of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: So I said: If she gives birth, then it is permissible. Her waiting period had ended, and Abu Hurairah said: I will say what, my nephew said, and Abu Salamah said: So we sent a scribe to Umm Salamah to ask her about That, then it came to us that Subayah “her husband died, and she gave birth a few days after her husband’s death, so the Messenger of God commanded her May God bless him and grant him peace, that you get married.”"
"5511","Abd Al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Ja’far bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abd al-Rahman, that Zainab bint Abi Salamah told him, on the authority of her mother, Umm Salama’s husband The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A woman from Aslam, called Subayah, was married to her husband, and he died while she was pregnant. Then Abu Al-Sanabel ibn Baakk proposed to her, but she refused to marry him. He said: It is not right for you to marry until you have passed the last of the two terms. So she stayed for about twenty nights, then she died and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Get married. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5512","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdul Razzaq informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Dawud bin Abi Asim informed me, That Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told him, saying: While Abu Hurairah and I were with Ibn Abbas, a woman came to him and said: Her husband died while she was pregnant, and she gave birth less than four months from the day he died. Ibn Abbas said: Bring the last of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that Subayah al-Aslamiyah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, and she said: “Her husband died while she was pregnant, so she gave birth less than four months ago, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her And peace be upon her to marry.” Abu Hurairah said: I bear witness to that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5513","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ubayd Allah bin Abdul God told him that his father wrote to Omar bin Abdullah bin Al-Arqam Al-Zuhri, ordering him to go to Subayah bint Al-Harith Al-Islamiyyah. Then he asked her about her speech and what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her when she asked him for advice. So Omar bin Abdullah wrote to Abdullah bin Utbah tells him that Subay’a told him: “She was under Saad bin Khawla, who was from Banu Amir bin Luay, and he was among those who A full moon witnessed, and her husband died on her behalf during the Farewell Hajj while she was pregnant. She did not wish to give birth after his death, so when she became pregnant, she As a result of her exhaustion, she became beautiful for Al-Khattab, so Abu Al-Sanabel bin Baakak, a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and said to her: Why do I see you so beautiful? Perhaps you want to get married. By God, you will not get married until four and ten months have passed for you. Subayah said: When he told me that I gathered my clothes in the evening, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about that, and he gave me a fatwa stating that I was permissible when I gave birth. He made me pregnant, and ordered me to get married if I wanted to.”"
"5514","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid bin Abi told me Unaisa, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, who wrote to him mentioning that Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told him that Zafar bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan Al-Nasri narrated to him that Abu Al-Sanabel bin Ba’ak bin Al-Sabbaq said to Subay’ah Al-Aslamiyyah, “Do not permissible until he passes.” You have four months and ten days, the maximum of the two terms. So she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about that. She claimed that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He gave her a fatwa to get married if she gave birth, and she was nine months pregnant when he died. Her husband, and she was married to Saad bin Khawla, so he died on her behalf during the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she married A young man from her people when she gave birth to what was in her stomach.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5515","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, That Abdullah bin Utbah wrote to Omar bin Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Arqam Al-Zuhri to enter the house of Subayah bint Al-Harith Al-Islamiyya, So ask her about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a fatwa regarding her pregnancy. He said: Then Omar bin Abdullah entered and asked her, So she told him, “She was with Saad bin Khawlah, and he was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and was among those who witnessed Badr. He died on her behalf during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and she gave birth before fourteen months had passed since the death of her husband. During her postpartum period, Abu al-Sanabel ibn Ba’ak, a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and saw her looking beautiful, so he said: Perhaps you want to get married before she Four and ten months had passed since you had lived. She said: When I heard that from Abu al-Sanabel, I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him what I had said. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You were lawful when you gave birth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5516","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, he said: I was He was sitting in a gathering in Kufa, in a large gathering of the Ansar, one of whom was Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila. They mentioned the matter of Subay’a, so I mentioned On the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, regarding the meaning of Ibn Aoun’s statement: Until she gives birth, Ibn Abi Laila said: But his uncle does not say that. So I raised my voice and said: I am bold to lie to Abdullah bin Utbah, while he was in the vicinity of Kufa. He said: I met Malik, so I said: What did Ibn Masoud say about Subayah? He said: He said: Do you impose a burden on her, and do not give her a concession, for Surat An-Nisa, the shorter one, was revealed after the tall one? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5517","Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Basri al-Yamami informed me, he said: Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, he said: Muhammad informed us, and Maymun ibn Al-Abbas Al-Raqqi, he said: Saeed bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told me, he said: Ibn Shubrumah Al-Kufi told me, On the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Qays, that Ibn Masoud said: “Whoever wills, his curse will not be sent down. And the first burdens are theirs.” That they give birth except after the sign of her husband whose husband has died. If the woman whose husband has died gives birth, then it is permissible.” And the wording is for “Maymun.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5518","Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Ayan, told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, and Muhammad bin told me Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Bukayr, told us, he said: Zuhair bin Muawiyah told us, he said: Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, Masruq, and Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, “Sura An-Nisa’ Al-Qusa was revealed after Al-Baqarah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5519","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that: “He was asked about a man who married a woman and did not impose a dowry for her, nor did he have intercourse with her. Until he died, and Ibn Masoud said: She is entitled to the dowry of her wives, no sex or excess, and she is required to observe the waiting period and she is entitled to the inheritance. So Maqil ibn Sinan stood up Al-Ashja'i, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has ruled among us regarding Barwa’ bint Washiq, one of our women, just as you have judged. So Ibn Al-Ashja’i was happy. Masoud, may God be pleased with him.”"
"5520","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for a woman to mourn more than three dead people, except for her husband.”"
"5521","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Sulayman bin Kathir told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to marry more than three days except for a pair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5522","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Ayoub bin Musa told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this on Al-Minbar: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and His Messenger to mourn a dead person for more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days.”"
"5523","Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Kufi told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, Ibn Jurayj, Yahya bin Saeed, and Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq. On the authority of Zainab bint Kaab, on the authority of Al-Fari’ah bint Malik, that her husband went out seeking treatment, and they killed him. Shu’bah and Ibn Jurayj said, and she was in a house. Far away, so she came and her two brothers came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they mentioned to him, so he granted her permission, and when she returned he invited her and said: “Sit in your house.” “Until the book reaches its term.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5524","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Yazid bin Muhammad, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, On the authority of his paternal aunt Zainab bint Kaab, on the authority of Al-Furai’ah bint Malik, that her husband was forced to work for him, so they killed him, so she mentioned that. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “I do not live in his residence, and I do not receive any sustenance from him. Should I move to my family and my orphans?” So I will stand up to them. He said: Do it. Then he said: How did you say? So she repeated her statement to him. He said: “Application as the news reaches you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5525","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Zainab, on the authority of Furay’ah, that her husband went out in search of A cure for him, and he was killed by the arrival. She said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned to him the transfer to my family, and I mentioned to him the situation. Regarding her condition, she said: He granted me permission, and when I came he disputed with me, saying: “Stay with your family until the appointed time has been fulfilled.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5526","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Warqa’ told us, meaning Ibn Omar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, Ata’ said, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “This verse is abrogated by her waiting period among her family, so she may observe the waiting period wherever she wishes. This is the saying of God Almighty: \Unextracted\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5527","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, he said: My paternal aunt Zainab bint Ka’b told me: Furay’ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, told me: “My husband died on arrival. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned to him that our house was large, so he gave her permission, then he called her and said: Stay in your house for four days. months and tens, until the book reaches its term.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5528","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, I read it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is by Muhammad, he said: Ibn Al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Bakr, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, that she told him these three hadiths, and Zainab said: I went to see Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when her father, Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, died. She called Umm Habiba with kindness. So a maid anointed him, then touched her private parts, then said: “By God, I have no need of perfume except that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him, he says: It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God, and on the Last Day, to mourn a dead person for more than three nights, except for a husband, four. \months and tens\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5529","Zainab said: Then I went to Zainab bint Jahsh when her brother died, and she had asked for perfume and she touched some of it, then she said: By God, I don’t have enough perfume. Of any need, except that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the pulpit: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day, “You must mourn a dead person for more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days.”"
"5530","Zainab said: I heard Umm Salamah saying: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, my daughter Her husband died, and her eye was suffering. Should I apply kohl to her? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” Then he said: It is only four months and ten, and one of you was during the pre-Islamic period. You throw a heifer at the beginning of the year.” Humaid said: So I said to Zainab: What do you throw with the dung at the time of the year? Zainab said: When a woman’s husband died, she would enter a boat, wear her best clothes, and would not touch perfume or anything until she passed by. One year, then an animal is brought, whether a donkey, a sheep, or a bird, and it is separated from it. It is not often that something is spread apart unless it dies. Then it is brought out and given to it. She throws it away, then takes it back after she wants of perfume or something else. Malik said: to cover oneself with it: to wipe oneself with it, and in the hadith of Muhammad, Malik said: the hafsh: the private parts. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5531","Hussein bin Muhammad al-Zarra’ al-Basri told us, he said: Khaled, he is Ibn al-Harith, told us, he said: Hisham, he is Ibn Hassan, told us, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiya, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should not mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband. She must mourn for him for four months and ten days, and she must not wear dyed clothing except dyed clothing, and she should not apply kohl, comb her hair, or touch herself. “It is good, except when it is purified, when it is purified, and it is free of calluses and nails.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5532","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn more than three dead people, except for a husband, and she should not use kohl. “Do not dye your hair, and do not wear dyed clothing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5533","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Makhramah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Mughirah bin Al-Dahhak says: Umm Hakim bint Usayd told me on the authority of her mother that her husband died and she was complaining about her eye, so she applied kohl to remove it. So she sent a female servant of hers to Umm Salamah and asked her about kohl for applying kohl, and she said: She should not use kohl except for something that is absolutely necessary for her. Ali came in. When Abu Salamah died, and I had placed patience on my eyes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is this, Umm Salamah? I said: It is it Patience, O Messenger of God. There is no perfume in it. He said: It makes the face look young, so do not apply it except at night, and do not comb with perfume or henna. It is dye. I said: With what should you comb it, O Messenger of God? He said: With a lot of Sidr to cover your head with.”"
"5534","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ayoub, who is the son of Musa, told us. Humaid said: Zainab bint Abi Salamah told me, on the authority of her mother, Umm Salamah. She said: “A woman from the Quraysh came and said: O Messenger of God, my daughter She turned red, should I use kohl for her and she had died? He said: Except for four months and ten. Then she said: I fear for her sight. He said: No, except for four months and ten days. In pre-Islamic times, one of you used to mourn her husband for a year and then stone the stones on New Year’s Day. \By the waste\"""""
"5535","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab bint Abu Salamah, on the authority of her mother, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him “about her daughter. Her husband died and she was complaining.” The same thing. He said: One of you used to mark the year, then throw the heifer at the beginning of the year, but it was only fourteen months. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5536","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa bin Maadan told us, he said: Ibn Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us On the authority of Humayd ibn Nafi’, the client of the Ansar, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that a woman from Quraysh came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: “My daughter’s husband died, and I feared for her eyes, and she wanted kohl.” He said: “It was “One of you throws a heap at the beginning of a year, but it is only four months and ten days.” So I said to Zainab: What is the beginning of a year? She said: In pre-Islamic times, when a woman’s husband died, she would go to the worst house of hers and sit there until a year had passed. She went out, leaving a wasteland behind her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5537","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad, he is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab, A woman asked Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah, “Should she use kohl during her waiting period due to the death of her husband?” They said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so I asked him about that, and he said: In the pre-Islamic era, if one of you had her husband die, she stayed in residence for a year, then She threw a dung after her, then she came out, but it is only four months and ten until the period expires.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5538","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: I am Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiya. On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “he granted permission to the woman whose husband died when she was purified with regard to the blood and the nails.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5539","Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Sijzi, the tailor of the Sunnah, told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim Rahawayh told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein told us Ibn Waqid, he said: My father told me, he said: Yazid the grammarian told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said in his saying: “And those Some of you die and leave behind wives, leaving behind a bequest to their wives for a year without taking them out, so that is abrogated by the verse on inheritance from what was imposed. It has a quarter and an eighth, and the term of the year was abrogated by making its term four months and ten.”"
"5540","Abdul-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin told me Asim, that Fatima bint Qais, the sister of Al-Dahhak bin Qais, informed him, and she was with a man from Banu Makhzum, that he had divorced her three times, and he left. He went to some battlefields, and he ordered his representative to give her some of the maintenance, so she took it, and she went to some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered while she was with her, and she said: O Messenger of God, “This is Fatima bint Qays, so-and-so divorced her, so he sent He went to her for some maintenance, but she returned it. He claimed that it was something he was trying too hard to do, and he said: He spoke the truth. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then go to Umm Kulthum, so he committed the waiting period with her, then he said: Umm Kulthum is a woman who often commits sexual intercourse, so go to Abdullah bin Umm Maktoum, for he Blind.” So she went to Abdullah bin Umm Maktoum, and she observed the waiting period with him until her waiting period was over, then Abu Al-Jahm proposed to her. And Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan. She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him to conspire over them. He said: As for Abu Al-Jahm, he is a man I fear. You have to harden him to the stick. As for Muawiyah, he was a man of wealth. She married Usama bin Zaid after that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5541","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Hujain told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, that she told him, “She was under the supervision of Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, So he divorced her, the last of three divorces, and she claimed that she had come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she asked him to ask him about her leaving her house. He ordered her to go to the blind house of Ibn Umm Maktoum.” Marwan refused to believe Fatima about the divorced woman leaving her house, Urwa said. : Aisha denied that to Fatima. Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Hafs told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Fatima, I said: O Messenger of God, “My husband has divorced me three times, and I fear that he will attack me, so he commanded her and she changed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5542","Yaqoub bin Mahan Al-Baghdadi told us, on the authority of Hushaym, he said: Sayyar, Husayn, Mughirah, and Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, And Ismail bin Abi Khaled, and another mentioned, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I entered upon Fatima bint Qays, and asked her about the decree of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless her and grant her peace, and she said: “Her husband divorced her once and for all, so she disputed with him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about housing and maintenance.” She said: He did not grant me housing or maintenance, and ordered me to observe the waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"5543","5588 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told me, Ahwas bin Al-Jawab told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Shaabi, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, said: “My husband divorced me, so I wanted to move, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Move.” To the house of your cousin Amr ibn Umm Maktoum, and perform the ritual there.” Al-Aswad looked at him and said: Woe to you, you have not given a fatwa like this. Omar said: If you bring two witnesses who will testify that they heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, otherwise we will not leave the Book of God to say Do not expel women from their homes or go out unless they commit a clear indecency."
"5544","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad al-Harrani told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ His aunt was divorced, so she wanted to go out to her palm trees, but she met a man who forbade her, so she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Go out. So find your palm trees, perhaps you will give charity and do a favor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5545","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Jahm, he said: Abu Salamah and I went to Fatima bint Qays, she said: “My husband divorced me and did not grant me housing or maintenance. She said: So he granted me Ten baskets of money were with a cousin of his: five barley and five dates. So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that. He said: He spoke the truth, and he commanded me to observe the waiting period in the house of so-and-so, and her husband had divorced her irrevocably. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5546","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar Al-Humsi told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Zuhri said, Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah told me that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan divorced the daughter of Sa`id ibn Zayd. Her mother was Hamnah bint Qais of course, so her aunt Fatima bint Qais ordered her to move from the house of Abdullah bin Amr, and he heard about that. Marwan, so he sent for her and ordered her to return to her place until her waiting period was over. So she sent to him informing him that her aunt Fatima gave her a fatwa about that, and told her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He gave her a fatwa about her transfer when Abu Amr bin divorced her.” Hafs Al-Makhzoumi, so Marwan sent Qubaysah bin Dhu’ayb to Fatima to ask her about that, and she claimed that she was under the supervision of Ubayy. Amr, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Ali bin Abi Talib to go to Yemen, he went out with him, so he sent to her with a divorce, and she The remainder of her divorce, and Al-Harith bin Hisham and Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah ordered her to support her, and she sent to Al-Harith and Ayyash She asked them about the maintenance that her husband had ordered her to pay, so they said: By God, she has no obligation to support us except that she is pregnant, and she does not have the right to live in a Our residence except with our permission. Fatima claimed that she had come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she mentioned that to him, so he believed them both. She said: So I said: Where should I go, O Messenger of God? He said: Go with Ibn Umm Maktum, who is the blind man whom God Almighty blamed in his book. So I moved with him, and I used to leave my clothes with him, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her. She claimed that Usama bin Zaid was the wife.”"
"5547","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, On the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, that Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh She told him that she had come to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she noticed the blood, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “It was That is a vein, so be careful. When your reading has come, do not pray. If your reading has passed, then purify yourself, then pray from one reading to another.”"
"5548","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, he said: My father told me, he said Yazid the grammarian told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “Whatever verse We abrogate or forget, We bring with it good.” Of it or something similar to it, and He said: And when We change a verse in place of another verse, and God knows best what He is sending down, and the Almighty said: God erases whatever He wills. And he is proven, and with him is the Mother of the Book: The first thing that was abrogated in the Qur’an was the qiblah, and God Almighty said: And divorced women should wait by themselves for three days. Read, and it is not permissible for them to conceal what God has created in their wombs, until His saying: if they want to reconcile, and that is because if a man divorces His wife, then he has more right to take her back, even if he divorced her three times, then he abrogated that, and said: Divorce twice, then withholding on a fair basis or releasing him. \With goodness\"""""
"5549","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Yunus bin Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Omar said: “I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Omar and mentioned that to him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Command him to take her back, and when she becomes pure,” meaning: “And if he wishes, let him divorce her.” I said to Ibn Umar: “So seek reward from her?” He said: What is stopping him? What do you think if he is unable and becomes foolish? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5550","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, and Yahya bin Saeed, and Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Zuhair, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, they said: “He divorced His wife was menstruating, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, mentioned it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Order him to take her back until she has another menstrual period. Then when she is pure, then if he wishes, he may divorce her, and if he wishes, he may keep her. This is the divorce that God Almighty has commanded. The Almighty said: So divorce them. For their waiting period (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5551","5558 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: When Ibn Umar was asked about the man He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he says: “As for him divorcing her one or two, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to He will have intercourse with her, then he will keep her until she has another menstrual period, then she will become pure, then he will divorce her before he touches her. As for him divorcing her three times, he may “You disobeyed God in what He commanded you to do regarding divorcing your wife, and your wife estranged you.”"
"5552","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Hanzalah told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that: “He divorced His wife was menstruating, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to go back to her.”"
"5553","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, Ibn Juraij told me, he said: Ibn Tawus told me, on the authority of his father, He heard Abdullah bin Omar being asked about a man who divorced his menstruating wife. He said: Do you know Abdullah? He said: Yes, he said: For “he divorced his menstruating wife, then ‘Umar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him the news, so he ordered him to He will review it until it is pure.” And I did not hear him add anything more than that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5554","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri informed us, saying: Yahya bin Adam informed us, on the authority of Yahya, and Amr bin Mansour informed us. Al-Nasa’i, he said: Sahl bin Muhammad Abu Sa’id told us, he said: I was informed on the authority of Yahya bin Zakaria, on the authority of Salih bin Salih, he is the son of Hayy. Al-Hasan’s father, and Ali bin Saleh Al-Kufi, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He “divorced Hafsa, then took her back” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5555","I am Ya’qub bin Ibrahim. He said: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman informed me. Al-Ansari, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land will have a reward for it, and what “Whoever eats the sweet things, he will have a reward for it.”"
"5556","7000 Shuaib bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever revives a land will have a reward for it, and as long as it is healthy, he will have a reward for it.” Ayyub and Abbad ibn Abbad disagreed with him. Servants"
"5557","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land will have a reward for it. “Or whatever the maids eat from it, it is for him charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5558","Ali bin Muslim told us, he said: Abbad bin Abbad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land will have a reward for it, and whatever the wild ones eat from it is for him.” \charity\"""""
"5559","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever revives a dead land that does not belong to anyone has more right to it.” “Hiwa bin Shurayh disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5560","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Haywa bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubair, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land that does not belong to anyone, it is his, and no race has any right.” “Unjust,” Muhammad said: Urwah said: The unjust race: the man who populates the desolate land, and it belongs to the people who were unable to control it, so they abandoned it until it became desolate. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5561","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land, it belongs to him, and not to an unjust race.” “Truth.” Yahya bin Sa’id and Laith bin Sa’d disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5562","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever revives a dead land, it belongs to him, and an oppressive race has no right.” Al-Layth said: Then I wrote to Hisham bin Urwa, so he wrote to me with a hadith similar to the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed."
"5563","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever surrounds whatever land he steps on, it belongs to him.”"
"5564","Saeed bin Amr told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Qais Al-Marbi, on the authority of Abyad bin Hammal Al-Mazni said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if the salt in Ma’rib would cut me off,” so he cut it off for me. He said A man: It is like running water, but he refused to let me cut it."
"5565","Sa`id bin Amr told us, he said: Baqiyya bin al-Walid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Qais al-Marbi, on the authority of Abyad bin Hammal said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I cut him off the salt that was in Ma’rib, and he cut it off for me, and a man said: O Messenger of God, it is like water for counting. He said: Then no. Sa`id bin Amr told us. He said: Baqiyyah told us, and Sufyan said, and he told me. Ibn Abyad bin Hammal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with something similar to him, Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak differed from him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5566","Abd al-Salam bin Atiq told us, he said: Muhammad bin al-Mubarak told us, he said: Ibn Ayyash and Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Qais Al-Marbi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abyad bin Hammal, said: “I extracted from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a mine of salt. The one in Ma'rib, so he cut it off, and it was said: It is like water for counting, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, then he attributed it. Muhammad bin Yahya bin Qais (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5567","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya bin Qais Al-Marbi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Thumama bin Sharahil, on the authority of Sumay Ibn Qays, on the authority of Shamir, on the authority of Abyad Ibn Hammal, “He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and salt cut it off, so it cut it off.” For him, and when he left, a man said: O Messenger of God, do you know what you have cut off for him? You only cut off his water count, so he took it back from him. He said, meaning: With plenty of water (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5568","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya bin Qais told us, he said: Abu Yahya bin Qais told me, on the authority of Thumama bin Sharahil, On the authority of Sumayy ibn Qays, on the authority of Shamir, on the authority of Abyad ibn Hammal, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “What is protected from arrak?” He said: “Unless the camel’s hoofs reach him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5569","Ishaq bin Ismail told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Sufyan said: I met Rabi’ah, and he said: Yazid, the servant of the Prophet, spoke to me. On the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was asked about lost camels, and he became angry and his cheeks turned red, so he said: What’s the matter with you? And she has shoes and a waterskin, and she can draw water and eat trees until her master meets her. He was asked about the lost sheep, and he said: Take them. “It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5570","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Asad told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed and Rabi’ah, On the authority of Yazid, the client of Al-Manba’th, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about lost camels, and he said: What do you have to do with her? She has her watering can and her shoes. Let her eat from the tree until her master meets her. He was asked about the lost sheep, and he said: Take it, for it is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5571","Ali ibn Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Al-Manbu’th, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid, that a man, who said He said: O Messenger of God, the lost sheep? He said: Take it, for it is yours, or your brother’s, or the wolf’s. He said: O Messenger of God, The waste of camels? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and said: What do you have to do with it when it has its shoes and water until it meets its Lord? Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid."
"5572","Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Whoever was pleased told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Asi, on the authority of Rabia bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, the client of Al-Manba’th, on the authority of A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “was asked about the stray, and he said: Know its protection and its protection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5573","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The surplus water is not withheld in order to withhold the herds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5574","Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris informed us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab ibn Jathama, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no fever except for God and His Messenger.” He was asked about people who spend the night and fall ill. “The boys,” he said: “They are one of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5575","Al-Mugheerah bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: “Hilal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a tithe of his bee, and asked him to He protects a valley called Salba, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, protected that valley for him. When Omar Ibn Al-Khattab took charge, Sufyan wrote Ibn Wahb went to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab asking him, so Omar wrote: If he gives you what he gave to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, of ten If it is destroyed, then protect its prey for him. Otherwise, it is only a rainfly, which whoever it pleases may eat.”"
"5576","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir told us, with dictation from his memorizers. He said: Hibban bin Hilal told us. He said: Hammam bin Yahya told us. He said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Safwan bin Ya`la bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When my messengers come to you, give them Thirty shields and thirty camels, so I said: O Messenger of God, a loan guaranteed, or a loan to be paid in return? He said: Rather a loan to be paid back?"
"5577","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir told us, dictating from his book, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He borrowed thirty horses from him. He said: And he calculated it. He said: Thirty camels. He said: O Messenger of God, a loan guaranteed or a loan to be paid in return? He said: Rather a loan to be paid in return? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5578","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He borrowed from Safwan Armor and horses. Safwan said: loaned or usurped. He said: Nay, loaned him between thirty and forty armor. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked Hunayn, and when God defeated the polytheists, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gather your armor. Safwan, and they lost some of his armor. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Safwan: If you wish, we can fine it for you. He said: O Messenger. “By God, there is more faith in my heart today than there was at that time.”"
"5579","I am Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umayyah bin Safwan bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He borrowed armor from him on the day of Hunayn, and said: Usurpation, O Muhammad? He said: Rather, it is a guaranteed loan. He said: Some of it was lost, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered to guarantee it for him. He said: I Today I desire the Messenger of God in Islam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5580","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, meaning Ibn Musa, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Safwan bin Umayyah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He borrowed armor from Safwan bin Umayyah, and he perished.” Some of them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you wish, we can fine them. He said: No, O Messenger of God."
"5581","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Al-Hajjaj bin Farafafah, he said: He told me Muhammad ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Abu Amer, on the authority of Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The naked thing shall be paid back, and the generous Performed. A man said: O Messenger of God, have you seen the covenant of God Almighty? He said: The covenant of God Almighty is the most worthy of what has been fulfilled. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5582","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Kharijah told us, he said: Al-Jarrah bin Malih told us, he is a Syrian, but not Abu Waki’, he said: Hatim bin Harith Al-Tai narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Umamah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The thing that is ungrateful will be paid back, and the goodness that is done will be rejected.”"
"5583","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “On the hand is what you take until you return it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5584","5924 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told me, he said: Muawiyah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, and Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram ibn Muhayyisah, on the authority of Al-Baraa, that a she-camel of the Al-Baraa family spoiled something, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided it. “And he recognized that the preservation of the fruits is the responsibility of its owners during the day, and the owners of the livestock are responsible for what their livestock spoils at night.”"
"5585","Amr ibn Uthman informed us on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Haram ibn Muhaiyya, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, He said: “He had a ferocious she-camel, and she entered a wall and spoiled it. He spoke to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, and he decided that Maintaining walls during the day is the responsibility of its people, and protecting livestock at night is the responsibility of its people, and the responsibility of the people of the livestock is the responsibility of “I walked with them at night.”"
"5586","Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Al-Abbas Al-Antaki told us, saying: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram bin Muhaiyyasa, on the authority of his father, said: “I spoiled the she-camel of Al-Baraa bin Aazib in the neighborhood of a people,” so it was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ruled that the livestock should be protected from their families at night, and the walls should be protected from their families during the day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5587","Muhammad bin Aqeel bin Khuwaylid informed us, he said: Hafs told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Maysarah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, “A she-camel of his fell into the wall of a people, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judged the It is the responsibility of those who own wealth to guard it during the day, and it is the responsibility of those who own livestock to guard it at night. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Muhammad bin Maysarah: He is Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa, and he is weak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5588","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The man is a tyrant.”"
"5589","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Fire is mighty.” Ahmad bin Saeed added, “And the well is mighty.”"
"5590","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, that people, from Banu Amir They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: We find the camels of camels, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Burn the stray of a Muslim. \fire\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5591","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The lost Muslim is burned by fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5592","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Al-Jariri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Muslim, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What a Muslim goes astray is burning fire, so do not approach it, three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5593","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The lost matter of a Muslim is the burning of fire, so do not approach it.” Shu’bah disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5594","5636 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, On the authority of Abu Muslim, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, he said: “We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were riding lean camels, so we said: O Messenger of God, We are passing by a place that he has named, and we find camels and we ride them. He said: The lost Muslim is the burning of fire."
"5595","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Abu Muslim, On the authority of Al-Jaroud, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The straying of a Muslim is the burning of fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5596","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed Al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Judhami, on the authority of Al-Jaroud ibn Al-Mu’alla, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about straying people,” and the Messenger of God said, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The lost matter of a Muslim is the burning of fire. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5597","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Al-Qanabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Muslim, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim’s misguidance is the burning of fire.” Jarir bin Hazim disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5598","Ahmad bin Amr told us, he said: I am bin Wahb, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Muslim, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of the straying of a Muslim, for it is the burning of fire.”"
"5599","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Jarir said: We were with Jarir on the hunt, and the cows were running, and he saw among them a cow that he disapproved of, so he ordered it to be expelled, then He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “No one can shelter a lost woman except one who is lost.”"
"5600","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Al-Mundhir told us, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Jarir, he said: I was with my father. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No one can shelter a lost woman except one who is lost.”"
"5601","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn al-Mundhir, on the authority of Jarir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “No one can give shelter to a lost animal except a lost person, and no one can take it except a lost person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5602","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, And Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about a lost item.” The camels? He said: What do you have to do with them? They have their water and their shoes. Let them eat from the trees and come to the water until someone seeking them comes to them. He was asked about the lost sheep. He said: Is it yours, or your brother’s, or the wolf’s? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5603","Ishaq bin Ismail told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Khalid Al-Juhani said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was asked about a lost camel, and he became so angry that his cheeks turned red, so he said: What’s the matter with you?” And she has shoes and a waterskin, and she can draw water and eat trees until her master meets her. He was asked about the lost sheep, and he said: Take them. “It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5604","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ismail, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that a man said: O Messenger of God, “the lost sheep?” He said: Take them, for they are yours, or your brother’s, or To the wolf, he said: O Messenger of God, what is the waste of camels? He became angry and said: What do you have to do with it when it has its shoes and its water? Her Lord will meet her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5605","Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith narrated to me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah Bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Yahya Bin Abdul-Rahman Bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Bin Uthman Al-Taymi, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “He forbade the Hajj’s sighting.”"
"5606","Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawadah, On the authority of Abu Salem Al-Jishani, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever takes a shot is He is lost, unless he recognizes it.”"
"5607","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali, he said: “It was Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah: When he fought with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he carried a spear with him, and when he returned he threw it out to carry it, and Ali said to him: “ I would mention this to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Do not do it, for if you do it, you will be there for it, and you will not carry a stray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5608","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, who is the shoe, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Iyadh bin Himar Al-Ashja’i, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever takes a shot, let people of justice bear witness, and let him protect Its possessions and its stewards, and he does not conceal it or hide it, so if its owner comes, he has more right to it, and if its owner does not come, then it is God’s money. He gives it to whomsoever He wills.”"
"5609","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala. , on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Iyadh bin Himar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “He was asked about the snapshot, and he said: It is known and not hidden, and it is not concealed. If its owner comes with it, it is his, otherwise it is God’s property.” He gives it to whomsoever He wills.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5610","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, he said: Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abi Muslim, on the authority of Al-Jaroud, said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his travels, and at noon a few people remembered Dhuhr among them. I said: O Messenger of God, I know what is sufficient for us in Dhuhr. He said: What is sufficient for us? I said: Dhud, meaning: we will come On them, so we spread their backs, so he said: No, the Muslim’s stray will be burned in the fire, so do not approach it three times. He said: You will find the stray and the stray. So recite it, and if you know it, perform it. Otherwise, it is the wealth of God that He gives to whomever He wills.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
